{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies","id":1022814,"title":"Custom Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-27T10:07:02-08:00","id":1022814,"title":"Custom Legacies","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ephemeral Wraiths</b></span><br /> There are many hot topic and heated discussions when it comes to souls, ghost, reincarnation and life after death. These points of view are as varied as the cultures that spawned them and even within cultures there are diverse beliefs. The study of death, ghosts and of the soul is an obsession for many different groups. Most never take this study past an academic curiously, a hobby or just a fanciful whim. They sit around and wonder about life beyond the grave and romanticize about reunions with lost loved ones. However there are the few that will take their studies further looking at the cause an effect, trying to come up with some rhyme or reason to explain what lies beyond. However they are stopped due to a lack of a true understanding of death.<br /> <br /> The awakened have learned to look beyond the lie and to start looking at the fundamentals of what it means to die. They break down the process and examine the pieces through the lenses of the different Arcana. Still very few of them can grasp the intricacies that surround the human soul and fail to look past their limited views defined by their own Arcana. The Moros have master the concepts of death, ghosts and the soul moving on to the topic of how to affect them. They know that they can heal the soul, harm it and even destroy it. The same goes for a ghost. Then there are those among their ranks that look to have an even closer understanding.<br /> <br /> There are multiple groups among the Moros, and other paths, that delve into the intricacies of the soul but three of these groups have taken their studies of the soul to extreme heights. The Tremere Lich whose only goal is to devour it to extend his own miserable life. The Shadowbinders that take a ghost and bind it to their soul for healing their soul, forcing the ghost to serve as a familiar during this time. Then there are the Ephemeral Wraiths, they wish to transform their essence into a hybrid form, a meshing of awakened being and that an Ephemeral Entity becoming a Ghost-Mage.<br /> <br /> The Wraiths, as that are called, do not look to control the soul or harm it in any way. Their goal is to understand it so that they may one day transform into a Ghost-Mage, the liches can get there but through a much darker path. Their studies begin with viewing the souls of the living, looking for the markers that will determine why a ghost can be formed upon a person\u2019s death. Studies show that not everyone that dies will become a ghost condemned to walk in twilight.<br /> <br /> As their studies progress they learn to strengthen these souls and to manipulate the souls of the living. They study ghosts in great detail to determine what makes them different than other ephemeral substances. What was triggered upon death that allowed them to form? They spend endless hour watching ghosts as they go about their bleak existence. They spend just as much time studying the souls of the living looking for the markings that will determine if a ghost will form after death. Then they study their on soul to see if they can foster such markings within themselves.<br /> <br /> The more that they study this phenomenon the deeper they discover the rabbit hole goes. They learn to tap into the souls of the living and the ghosts of the dead, not harming them but to get a deeper understanding of their existence. They learn to influence the subjects of their studies in subtle way as to not disrupt their existence. They learn why a ghost is dammed to walk the earth and why some are force into an endless loop repeating the same task over and over again. Learning that the anchor they are tied to can also be manipulated, changed or even replaced. They are searching for what happens to a soul upon death, there are those that would say that it is destroyed and just as many that say it is releases to a realm that is beyond our comprehension. Whatever happens to it the mage knows that it can no longer be manipulated by awakened magic, therefore all intents and purposes it is gone.<br /> <br /> Finally they learn to transform their own twilight infused ephemeral substance into that of a ghost while still maintaining their own awakened abilities. They learn how to avoid the endless droning existence of the ghost. They have reached the pinnacle of their existence and have gained power over it. But they also discover that there studies do not end there. There is more than just existing in the twilight but for those answers they must travel to the Underworld and that frightens them to the core of their new existence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Moros, The Mysterium<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Wraiths; Half-Souled (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> No one really knows where and even why this Legacy started or ended, as records were shallow at best, but their demise was around 300 BCE. However early in the 15th century the studies began again. The heart of the Legacy sprang up in London and it has been growing ever since. Over the years since it's resurrection it has been suggested that this Legacy was originally part of the Pancryptiates and was defunct during the struggles between the Keepers of the Word and the Pancryptiates. Reportedly this group was primarily dedicated to finding a way for the Pancryptiates to leave the sleeping world behind. It is also believed that they might have been one of the \u201cHand of the Mind\u201d that was stealing knowledge from the other orders to further the goals of the Pancryptiates, this could have been responsible for their downfall and eventual dissolution.<br /> <br /> Since its revival the group has been under the watchful eye of the other orders, and there has been some debate as to the morality factor of this group. There are those that would say that the Legacies obsession with the transformation has lead them down the Left Hand Path, fearing that they will end up following the path of the Tremere Liches. Some say that their practices and core beliefs are nowhere near that of the Tremere and the other Left Hand Legacies. For the most part they are being watched and put on a tight leash their every move scrutinized for the slightest impropriety.<br /> <br /> The heart of the order has remained in London since its rebirth and is thriving well there. And it is needless to say but the Ephemeral Wraith and the Tremere Liches are not on good terms.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Wraith come from all walks of life, from the rich to the poor, the noble to the peasant, male, female, young and the old. Even though they can come from any nationality their numbers are mainly European, this is expected to change as the practice becomes more widely spread.<br /> <br /> As they start into this Legacy their skin takes on an ashen hue and their body looks ever so slightly gaunt. As they progress through the ranks, and with each attainment, these conditions worsen until they reach the fifth attainment. By this time they are unmistakably pale and they take on a more emaciated look. To the trained eye there is no doubt what is happening, to the layman he looks sickly. Where do you think the saying \u201cHe looks like he has one foot in the grave\u201d came from.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Death 2, and either Intimidation 2, Medicine 2 or Investigation 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> An extended and meaningful interview with a sick and dying person and with a ghost.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> The relative recent revival of this legacy makes it hard to form any unified organization, however the majority of the Legacy are in London where they have formed a council to deal with major issues. They try not to interfere with the lives and studies of their members as this style of study is very personal. They do have functions and collect fees for their services to members and non-members alike.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> There is a delicate balance between life and death. There is also some correlation between a soul and a ghost that is stuck in twilight. Just what the correlation is remains the topic of discussion within this Legacy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Death<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Ephemera (Legacy tool +1), Soul Jar (empty +1 or full +2), Viewing the soul of the subject (Persona +2), Funeral Shroud (Legacy Tool +1), A coin recovered from a corpse who\u2019s soul never crossed the river Styx (Legacy Tool +2).<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Extensive study of death rituals in different cultures; Studies of the different beliefs of the afterlife; hours of watching a ghost; Extended viewing of a living soul; Contemplating in a place where a death occurred; Wandering in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> The attainments of this Legacy show the different levels of understanding. They are the culmination of years of personal study. They start with the viewing of souls and ghosts into the direct contact with them, culminating with the transformation into a Ghost-Mage the ultimate goal of all in this Legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b> Soul Sight<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> The initiate uses this spell on an almost continuous basis, as he studies both the souls of the living and the dead. This attainment enables the initiate to see, but not interact with, the souls of the dead and living alike. They can use the effects of Soul Marks when viewing these souls. This is always done as an instant casting and may determine one of the following per level of potency. She can discern the presence of Persistent Conditions, if the subject is Awakened, if the subject is a supernatural being, if the subject has created a soul stone (see \u201cSoul Stones\u201d p. 98), if the subject has had her soul tampered with, if the subject is Possessed, the presence of any Gnosis 5+ Legacy Attainments, if the subject has eaten or otherwise consumed another\u2019s soul, or if the subject is suffering from a Paradox Condition. Reach used is for instant casting.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 1<br /> The initiate can also gain information about the target by studying its connections to the Supernal. Even though the information gathered isn\u2019t specifically tied to death or the soul it is still useful information to have. This attainment enabler the initiate to gain the abilities of the Supernal Vision spell. Reach used is for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b> Produce Ectoplasm<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Death 2<br /> The apprentice can produce ectoplasm from his mouth, regurgitating the thick slimly substance. This ectoplasm is identical to that left by a manifested ghost and is crucial in the understanding of the ghost phenomenon. Once produced he can shape it into any form that he wants and it will remain in that form until the spell ends or he reshapes it again. The attainment enables him to produce the same effects as the spell Ectoplasm. Reach used is for instant casting.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 2<br /> Instead of Concentrating on a ghost the initiate with this variant is concentrating on twilight itself. This is to determine if it is twilight itself that hold the power to form ephemera into a ghost when a person dies. By studying the ebbs and flows of power he can see the flow of energy and how it interacts with the ephemera. This variant enables the initiate to use the abilities of the Sacred Geometry spell. Reaches used is for instant casting and to determine if the node sits atop of a hollow.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment:</b> Travel on Death\u2019s Trail<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 4, Death 3<br /> A disciple at this level of understanding can enter and leave Twilight on a whim. You can only fully understand something and if you have walked a mile in its shoes. The attainment enables the disciple the ability to enter twilight as the spell Ghost Gate except that he turns his body and items into the ephemera of twilight instead of opening a gate. This ability requires a full scene to activate. Reach used is for not needing a gate.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 3<br /> The dangers of being in twilight are all too real and the smart disciple is prepared to hide if need be. He can also hide others when the need arises making him a valuable ally no matter what realm he is in. This variant allows the disciple the use of the Supernal Veil spell. Reaches used is for instant casting and Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:</b> Strengthen Ghost<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6, Death 4<br /> An adept can do some truly amazing feats and gets a greater level of understanding of the weakness of the ghost. He learns to bargain with the ghost to offer it increased power, albeit for a limited amount of time. This attainment enables the mage to strengthen the ghost\u2019s ephemeral substance as if using the Quicken Ghost spell. This attainment costs one mana as the mage also raises the rank of the ghost by 1. He must touch the ghost and he must spend a point of mana. Reach used is for instant casting and to raise rank by 1.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 4<br /> At this level the adept is capable of some horrific damage should the need arise to defend himself. This variant allows the adept to call forth Celestial Fire tainted with the Death-attuned energies of twilight. This fire burn with cold energies and takes on the appearance of a dark swirling vortex. This variant enables the Adept to call upon the Celestial Fire spell. Reach used is for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b> Death\u2019s True Form<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 8, Death 5<br /> A master\u2019s level of understanding is unmatched and he is truly an authority in the field. At this level he can actually transform his Ephemeral Form gained by entering Twilight into an Ephemeral Entity. This Entity is none other than a ghost. This transformation is especially awe inspiring as he still has access to all the abilities, including magical abilities, while in this form. This attainment enables the master to use the abilities of the Ghost Form spell (listed below). He may spend the reaches in any manner that he sees fit as each master\u2019s view of their ghost form is different. Be careful as there are still things that roam in that realm that are bigger and more terrifying than you. This is an instantaneous transformation and has advanced duration.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 5<br /> The Master versed in prime can use this variant to enchant the very ephemera of the twilight. The subject of the spell can affect beings and objects in twilight as if he were in twilight. He can enchant an ephemeral object that is a weapon and that weapon will act as a bane to the entity so attacked with it. This variant enables the master to gain the effects of the Ephemeral Enchantment spell. Reaches used is for instant casting and to enchant a weapon.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>New Spells:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Vision (Death \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult.<br /> The mage can gaze into the very Ephemeral of all that reside in the Death-attuned Twilight. The mage must have the ability to see into Twilight albeit by magical or by actually being there. By studying an Ephemeral patterns of an entity or object the mage can gather information as to its general abilities and condition. The mage must study the pattern for a minimum of one turn after which he can gather certain information about it. For each level of potency that mage can ask one of the following questions.<br /> \u2022 What is the Rank of the entity?<br /> \u2022 How many manifestation does it have?<br /> \u2022 What one of its manifestations? * This question may be asked more than once.<br /> \u2022 What is its General level of decay?<br /> \u2022 Is the pattern bleeding essence?<br /> \u2022 What is its Ban<br /> \u2022 What is its Bane<br /> The symbols of death and decay start to appear around the entity or object. The subject may continue to study the Ephemera and continue to get more answers as long as the spell lasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Splice Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstanding:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidate, Medicine, Occult.<br /> For the duration of this spell the mage can splice a sliver of his soul onto that of a Living soul. The target must be a sleeper and for the duration of this spell he temporarily becomes a sleepwalker with all that entails. Any breaking points due to witnessing magic and Quiescence effects the subject would normally suffer are held in abeyance until the spell\u2019s Duration expires, only to come crashing down all at once when the spell ends.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> As long as the spell\u2019s Duration lasts, its wielder may spend one point of Mana at any time to \u201crecharge\u201d this effect, and the sleeper remains a sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Form (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Empathy, Survival.<br /> This spell allows the mage to transform a subject from twilight state into an Ephemeral Entity known as a ghost. For the duration of the spell the subject has the following traits determined by the mage at the time of casting. If the subject was a mage they use mana to power their abilities and they keep the Arcana ratings that they have, otherwise the newly formed ghost uses essence to power its abilities.<br /> <b><i>Drawbacks:</i></b> This power comes with a price. For every hour that the subject remains in ghost form they must roll Power + Resolve + Gnosis - 1 per previous roll. If they fail they start to become disconnected to their former self gaining the Driven condition (see below). If they ever dramatically fail this roll they gain the Amnesia condition forgetting there previous existence believing that they truly are just a ghost.<br /> <br /> <b>Driven Condition:</b> (persistent)<br /> Your character loses interest in everything except one task. This could be brought on by a tragedy, a mental break, or a spell gone tragically wrong. Whatever the reason your character loses interest in everything not related to fulfilling their goal.<br /> <b><i>Game Effect:</i></b> Your character loses interest in the current task at hand in favor of a new task which they will single mindedly peruse. All rolls not related to their new task is at a -2 dice.<br /> <b><i>Resolution:</i></b> Accomplish the goal.<br /> <b><i>Beat:</i></b> Character fails to fulfill an obligation due to pursuing her task.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Traits:</b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Power, Finesse, and Resistance:</b> Average the dots in each category to arrive at the new rating for each.<br /> <b>Influence:</b> The mage assigns what the ghost has influence over, this influence is at rank 2.<br /> <b>Twilight Form:</b> The ghost has the Twilight Form manifestation.<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> The mage may assign 2 additional manifestation (page 258 \u2013 261 or Chronicles of Darkness page 133 - 136) of his choice on the ghost.<br /> <b>Numina:</b> The mage may assign 3 Numina (page 261 \u2013 263 or Chronicles of Darkness page 136 - 138) of his choice to the ghost.<br /> <b>Essence/Mane Max:</b> 15<br /> <b>Bans:</b> The mage assigns a ban to the ghost.<br /> <b>Banes:</b> The mage assigns one bane to the ghost.<br /> All other traits listed on page 256 are calculated accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-30-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:09:05-08:00","id":1022816,"title":"","content":"Copied over from another thread<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/924832-wyrd-s-legacies-hub?p=1022807#post1022807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better would be to make separate topic and just mark me in post by writing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> in it - this topic is for organization of my own updates, only. But since you wrote in it, I may gives you some advises for your rewrote of Legacy.<br /> <br /> 1. You are sure of no Parent Order? They sounds as Mysterium obsessed guys.<br /> 2. Over specialization of Legacy. Maybe you should choose other Arcanum to accompany Death one? Because it's about souls and retaining magic - maybe Prime as second Arcanum?<br /> 3. If they are Liche Legacy ( about immortality ) I would add to their history some debate about them being Left-Handed and other Awakened telling that once completely Ghost, they are not truly themselves.<br /> 4. In Attainments write ups mark if particular action is Instant and what is Ritual. Good is also sum up on where Reaches goes from spell Attainments is based.<br /> <br /> Rethink those ideas and rewritten, post Legacy in new topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:11:17-08:00","id":1022819,"title":"","content":"Copied over from another thread<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/924832-wyrd-s-legacies-hub?p=1022804#post1022804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souls and ghosts aren't the same thing. Also, only Rank 1 ghosts are stuck in loops. Also, this legacy is a kind of lichdom, the Tremere are far from exclusive in that category. It's fine for your own game, but typically real historical figures aren't assumed to be part of any splat's particular background in order to leave as much room for the ST as possible. It doesn't look like you understand the Concept section's purpose. An attainment that has to contend with Withstand usually isn't a great choice since it won't usually work until you have higher levels in the arcana. The 2nd attainment is redundant with the Death 2 utility attainment, there should be a part of the 3rd attainment that clarifies that it takes a scene to activate, all Reach costs must be fixed when an attainment is formed so the 4th attainment doesn't work. What about the Optional attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:22:00-08:00","id":1022824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/924832-wyrd-s-legacies-hub?p=1022809#post1022809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts are dead souls that have not crossed over into the underworld and therefor become ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect, souls and ghosts are not the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:11:35-08:00","id":1022887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies#post1022814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They figure out that the soul of the living is the same as the soul of the dead, the only difference is that the body is the anchor living soul. That anchor is just as susceptible to manipulation as that of a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this the sentence that you are referring to, if it is then all I can say is that I do not know what the game material says about ghosts and souls but in many cultures Ghost are the souls of the dead that never crossed the river Styx. There is also a popular cultural belief that Ghosts are psychic residue left behind when a human was killed in a horrible or tragic way. There are those that believe that ghost are here to finish so unfinished business. There are those that believe that there are multiple soul in the body and that upon the death of the person one soul goes on to the afterlife and one soul stays in the body. <br /> <br /> I will change the sentence and any other such passages until I can find a answer one way or the other in the books for this game. Do you know which one of the cultural beliefs listed is supported by the game mechanics so that I can get it right. I would not want to change it to another one of the beliefs and still be wrong.<br /> <br /> Also do you realize that it is fluff text and there is no mechanical meaning behind fluff text. If the fluff text was written by someone of Chinese decent that could have easily stated the that &quot;It is known that the two souls residing in the body separate upon the death The Hun soul goes on to the afterlife and the Po soul stays with the body&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-27-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:26:07-08:00","id":1022894,"title":"","content":"In many cultures that might be the common belief, but Mage's know that they're not the same thing. Mages don't know what happens to your soul when you die. They know it disappears and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:32:05-08:00","id":1022898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies?p=1022894#post1022894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many cultures that might be the common belief, but Mage's know that they're not the same thing. Mages don't know what happens to your soul when you die. They know it disappears and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ok thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:14:35-08:00","id":1022920,"title":"","content":"The opening text is changed I will be sifting through the rest of the text to remove any references of that and to implement the suggested mage by <b>wyrdhamster</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:32:34-08:00","id":1022926,"title":"","content":"And all the other stuff I mentioned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:50:58-08:00","id":1022938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies?p=1022926#post1022926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all the other stuff I mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still working on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:27:40-08:00","id":1022952,"title":"","content":"Issued addressed.<br /> <br /> From wyrdhamster<br /> <br /> Parent Order: Changed to Mysterium<br /> <br /> Over Specialization of Death Arcanum: Looking into this, just not sure which Arcanum would be best to have as a secondary Arcanum. Prime looks good I just want to see how that would fit with the Attainments.<br /> <br /> Left Hand or Not: I have added a paragraph to the history section about being watched and being compared to the other left hand Legacies.<br /> <br /> Assigning the reaches to the attainments: Assigned the reaches.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> From Mrmdubois<br /> <br /> Ghost not soul: I have changed the wording of the introduction to remove all references that ghosts are souls.<br /> <br /> Lichdom: Added history to cover the debate as to is they are left hand<br /> <br /> Historical Figure: Removed reference to historical figure.<br /> <br /> Concept: Removed the concept portion as there doesn\u2019t seem to be a concept section in the Eleventh Question and I am using them as a guideline.<br /> <br /> 4<sup>th</sup> Attainment: Changed out the attainment for Quicken Ghost. Adding the reaches.<br /> <br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> Attainment: The second attainment clearly states that it is based off of the spell Touch of the Grave. I do not see the conflict as the spell is different from the 2<sup>nd</sup> level utility attainment. Added the reach expenditure.<br /> <br /> 3<sup>rd</sup> Attainment: Added \u201cThis ability requires time to activate, the same amount of time as a ritual.\u201d<br /> <br /> 4<sup>th</sup> Attainment: Changed out the attainment for Quicken Ghost. Adding the reaches.<br /> <br /> 5<sup>th</sup> Attainment: Added \u201cThis is an instantaneous transformation and has advanced duration.\u201d<br /> <br /> Optional Attainment: I was unaware that all Attainments of all Legacies requires Optional Attainments of Optional Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:41:41-08:00","id":1022962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies?p=1022952#post1022952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Issued addressed.<br /> <br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> Attainment: The second attainment clearly states that it is based off of the spell Touch of the Grave. I do not see the conflict as the spell is different from the 2<sup>nd</sup> level utility attainment. Added the reach expenditure.<br /> <br /> 3<sup>rd</sup> Attainment: Added \u201cThis ability requires time to activate, the same amount of time as a ritual.\u201d<br /> <br /> Optional Attainment: I was unaware that all Attainments of all Legacies requires Optional Attainments of Optional Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd attainment: It's not that there's a conflict, it's that they do almost exactly the same thing, literally the only thing turning Touch of the Grave into an attainment gives you is the ability to sense anchors, but you can do that with Death Mage Sight already, so it's a waste of an attainment.<br /> <br /> 3rd attainment: It takes a scene to activate (Usually at the end of a ritual but not the same kind as is normally done to cast a spell in ritual time), not the same amount of time as a ritual.<br /> <br /> Optional Attainment: Not all legacies require it, but it's a pretty big benefit to just ignore and could lead to it becoming an unpopular choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:52:43-08:00","id":1022972,"title":"","content":"It also allows me to grab Ephemeral Objects which I believe that the second level utility attainment doesn't correct. The second level utility attainment cost a mana if I decide I want to touch the ghost and the Touch of the Grave doesn't correct? I can change it but to what and I would like to keep the feel for the attainment. I also noticed that some Attainments have multiple effects is this common and should I be looking at doing that as well?<br /> <br /> I am open to suggestions for the Optional Attainments, By optional I am assuming that you are referring to the Optional Arcana that is at the end of some of the Attainments. I don't mind adding them but i have no Idea what i would like them to be, I also do not know what I should make as a secondary Arcana to this Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T16:03:16-08:00","id":1023012,"title":"","content":"Just some thoughts I will need to define them and such but this is the start anyway.<br /> <br /> 1st attainment:<br /> Optional Arcane: Prime 1 Supernal Vision<br /> <br /> 2nd attainment:<br /> Optional Arcane: Prime 2 Sacred Geometry<br /> <br /> 3rd attainment:<br /> Optional Arcane: Prime 3 Supernal Veil<br /> <br /> 4th attainment:<br /> Optional Arcane: Prime 4 Celestial Fire<br /> <br /> 5th attainment:<br /> Optional Arcane: Prime 5 Ephemeral Enchantment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-27-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:12:20-08:00","id":1023036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies?p=1022972#post1022972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also allows me to grab Ephemeral Objects which I believe that the second level utility attainment doesn't correct. The second level utility attainment cost a mana if I decide I want to touch the ghost and the Touch of the Grave doesn't correct? I can change it but to what and I would like to keep the feel for the attainment. I also noticed that some Attainments have multiple effects is this common and should I be looking at doing that as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be assumed that if you spend the point of mana via the Death 2 attainment to become physical to ghosts you'd likewise become physical to ephemeral objects thought you probably can't pull them from Twilight. Regardless, if you can't, that's a very niche benefit for taking Touch of the Grave as an attainment, and the cost of a point of mana is pretty negligible. Why not take Ectoplasm instead? Then you also get to shape what you're using.<br /> <br /> What do you mean by multiple effects for attainments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:45:45-08:00","id":1023045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies?p=1023036#post1023036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can be assumed that if you spend the point of mana via the Death 2 attainment to become physical to ghosts you'd likewise become physical to ephemeral objects thought you probably can't pull them from Twilight. Regardless, if you can't, that's a very niche benefit for taking Touch of the Grave as an attainment, and the cost of a point of mana is pretty negligible. Why not take Ectoplasm instead? Then you also get to shape what you're using.<br /> <br /> What do you mean by multiple effects for attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ectoplasm would work I will give it some thought.<br /> <br /> I realize that this is a 1e Legacy but Perfected Adept first level attainment has Body Control and Supernal Vision, thus two different effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T18:36:16-08:00","id":1023059,"title":"","content":"That's just an example of the fact that they didn't have standardized formatting for legacies. Technically the 1st Attainment should have been Body Control with an Optional Arcana of Prime that grants Supernal Vision.<br /> <br /> By the way, I understand that Soul Marks is appropriate to the legacy but it really sucks as a first attainment because of having to contend with Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-27-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T19:06:37-08:00","id":1023065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies?p=1023059#post1023059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just an example of the fact that they didn't have standardized formatting for legacies. Technically the 1st Attainment should have been Body Control with an Optional Arcana of Prime that grants Supernal Vision.<br /> <br /> By the way, I understand that Soul Marks is appropriate to the legacy but it really sucks as a first attainment because of having to contend with Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the explination, the legacies are difficult to figure out. And bummer about the Souls Marks being Whithstand.<br /> <br /> I did replace the second level attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T01:57:08-08:00","id":1023157,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that the Soul marks could be replaced with a death attuned spell that would give information about Ephemera (similar to Supernal Vision). Thoughts? I do not want to step on the toes of Supernal Vision so I tried to stay away from question dealing with powers like Numina, but I felt that Manifestation were fair game.<br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Vision (Death \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult.<br /> The mage can gaze into the very Ephemeral of all that reside in the Death-attuned Twilight. The mage must have the ability to see into Twilight albeit by magical or by actually being there. By studying an Ephemeral patterns of an entity or object the mage can gather information as to its general abilities and condition. The mage must study the pattern for a minimum of one turn after which he can gather certain information about it. For each level of potency that mage can ask one of the following questions.<br /> \u2022 What is the Rank of the entity?<br /> \u2022 How many manifestation does it have?<br /> \u2022 What one of its manifestations? * This question may be asked more than once.<br /> \u2022 What is its General level of decay?<br /> \u2022 Is the pattern bleeding essence?<br /> \u2022 What is its Ban<br /> \u2022 What is its Bane<br /> The symbols of death and decay start to appear around the entity or object. The subject may continue to study the Ephemera and continue to get more answers as long as the spell lasts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T02:07:32-08:00","id":1023159,"title":"","content":"It looks like a Death version of Know Spirit which still has to deal with Withstand.<br /> <br /> By the way I want to clarify something, Soul Marks and other similar spells that can be Withstood not being good as attainment is my bias because I don't like the idea of an attainment being able to fail, but by Death 3 it ought to work on most targets (Albeit with only one or two Potency requiring multiple activations to get all possible information). As you gain in Death obviously it becomes even more reliable although it could still prove useless against any 6+ Power Stat splat since their maximum attributes ceiling is higher. If that happens though the option remains to cast Soul Marks as a spell and increase Potency enough to beat such high Withstand. I don't like it, but I figure I should say as much so you can consider it yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T02:12:16-08:00","id":1023160,"title":"","content":"But I can see the logic behind the withstand dislike in an attainment. The supernal Vision spell that I was basing it on doesn't have a withstand. But if it needs a withstand then that is the way it is. It would still be a nice spell even if it isn't as useful to be used as an attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T03:10:38-08:00","id":1023174,"title":"","content":"You may have modeled it after Supernal Vision but it works exactly the same as Know Spirit which does have a Withstand, probably because it grants knowledge of an ephemeral entities greatest weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Looking at the 11Q in the book the Matter Optional has a pretty good effect that allows you to pierce Veils or mundane means of covering things up by scoring automatic successes equal to Matter dots. I assume this means auto-successes on Clashes of Will too which means they'd probably be able to pierce most forms of Matter appropriate deception with ease. You could do the same with Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-28-2016, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T03:17:43-08:00","id":1023176,"title":"","content":"I have finished adding the Optional Arcanum to the various attainments see what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:06:14-08:00","id":1023183,"title":"","content":"Looks good, but I'd make Supernal Veil spend a Reach for Advanced Duration instead of Advanced Scale. Getting allies together in a group hug is enough to effect at least 3 other people with basic Scale. You can also spam activate it just touch each ally before activating it since there's nothing stopping you from having multiple instances of an attainment going at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:13:56-08:00","id":1023185,"title":"","content":"True I was debating between Duration and scale<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:37:41-08:00","id":1023236,"title":"","content":"Day later, I think Legacy looks promising - I even thinking about adding one member to my own London game, so good work <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I only want to point one thing from history of Orders that may make it even cooler - Legacy could hail from predecesors of Mysterium. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies#post1022814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Background:</b> No one really know how or even why the Wraiths started only that it was before the inquisition. When the church established doctrine about death and the number of Wraiths dropped drastically. With few to preserve their ways they fell victim to the murderous and thieving ways of the Tremere Liches. There libraries and history all but lost to theft and destruction it is difficult at best to piece it all together. However early in the 15th century the studies began again. The heart of the Legacy sprang up in London and it has been growing ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just look over <b>DaveB</b>'s post on one of Order that created Mysterium as it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pancryptiates were smaller, weirder, and much more gnostic. They believed Sleepers actively damaged the world by existing, and sought to either remove themselves from the world and society or build bulwarks where the Abyss had less sway. The Keepers regarded all knowledge as at least partially magical - the Pancryptiates would be outraged by a Keeper storehouse keeping roman crop management manuals alongside the grimoires. They built demesnes, summoned supernal entities, studied the Abyss, explored Emanations and sought a way *out* of the Fallen World. They were like a cross between the Mysterium, Guardians, Arrow (they relished self-sacrifice for the cause, like becoming savants or jettisonning all mortal ties) and, in some ways, Tremere - they were deeply interested in the soul, and thought the world was evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to have quick look on the matter from <b>Mage</b> setting and in more books to dwell, I advise reading <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakened</a> topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-28-2016, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:48:00-08:00","id":1023269,"title":"","content":"I will start reading the Pancryptiates in The Mysterium book now. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .<br /> <br /> after looking at the material it does look promising, But I would want that information to be sketchy and loosely related at best, there could be a reference that suggests the Legacy was defunct from the early days of the struggle between the Keepers of the Word and the Pancryptiates.<br /> <br /> I will see what I can come up with, it would be nice if we could get DaveB to come in here and take a look. I would like to here it straight from him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-28-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:39:32-08:00","id":1023628,"title":"","content":"I want to that everyone especially Mrmdubois for your assistance in making this legacy into something that not only looks like it will work but into something that thematically will work into the rest of the CoD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDITED:</b> I was able to add the Pancryptiates into the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-29-2016, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:04:49-08:00","id":1024033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies#post1022814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Background:</b> No one really knows where or even why this Legacy started only that it was before the fall of the Roman empire. However early in the 15th century the studies began again. The heart of the Legacy sprang up in London and it has been growing ever since. Over the years since it's resurrection it has been suggested that this Legacy was originally part of the Pancryptiates and was defunct during the struggles between the Keepers of the Word and the Pancryptiates. Reportedly this group was primarily dedicated to finding a way for the Pancryptiates to leave the sleeping world behind. It is also believed that they might have been one of the \u201cHand of the Mind\u201d that was stealing knowledge from the other orders to further the goals of the Pancryptiates, this could have been responsible for their downfall and eventual dissolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a little nitpick on Background section - Diamond Orders, almost certainly, started in Roman Republic as proper organisations. It's not stated obviously in sources, but it's logical implication of 1E source materials and 2E official facts of setting ( like Adamantine Arrow was created before 200 BCE or that Seers of Throne where uncovered around 20 BCE, on rise of Roman Empire ). As it is, it's almost certin to assume that Awakened have all needed lore of what come from 20 BCE, at least on Diamond side. If this Legacy is from this period - there <i>will </i>be records of what they did then, maybe in old Keepers of Words journals ( they needed to understand their enemies in Pancryptiates ).<br /> <br /> If Legacy is way older, it could be hailing from much more older teaching, but they would forbade even Pancryptiates as Order. Remember, they did not become coherent Order at least past time of Alexander Empire, circa 300 BCE. In f<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">anon take</a> I started Keepers of the World from Great Library of Alexandria cult in years past 300 BCE, so if Legacy would be defunct, they should be <i>even</i> older. Hell, Phoenix Brethren idea of Gnostikon mages Darshana is even older than proper Keepers of the World Order ( Phoenix Brethren is just till 300 BCE ). Pancryptiates were mainly Asian mages ( Persians and Indian ), so maybe from those cults they come? Could be interesting to look in beliefs of those cultures for historical story hooks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:43:52-08:00","id":1024050,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Do they would have been defunct before 300 BCE for there to be little to not records of them correct?<br /> <br /> <br /> Change it slightly to place the time prior to 300 BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-29-2016, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:25:33-08:00","id":1024166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1022814-custom-legacies?p=1024050#post1024050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Do they would have been defunct before 300 BCE for there to be little to not records of them correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basicly - yes. Panscryptias are not known for keeping extensive records ( they were more 'direct experience' type of guys ) and before 300 BCE there would be still no Keepers of the Word to make archives on them.<br /> <br /> Only small nitpick - sentence: 'No one really knows where or even why this Legacy ended only that the end was prior to most of the recorded records of the time, that would place it around 300 BCE.'<br /> <br /> In to simply:<br /> 'No one really knows where and even why this Legacy started or ended, but any of tiny records are from time around 300 BCE would place it demise there.'<br /> <br /> Original sentence construction makes even my English cringe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-30-2016, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:12:35-08:00","id":1024214,"title":"","content":"LOL, thanks. I like it and adjust it only a little to this<br /> <br /> No one really knows where and even why this Legacy started or ended, as records were shallow at best, but their demise was around 300 BCE.<br /> <br /> English was never my best subject in school, mine was math and science. So my grammar, spelling and sentence structure is weak. My reading comprehension is strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-30-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:29:28-08:00","id":1024219,"title":"","content":"Best to admit the fault and try to fix it. My written English still is weak sometimes, but I try to make better all the time here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:31:53-08:00","id":1024220,"title":"","content":"It isn't bad so you should be proud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","